CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.6 (2026-10)
-------------------------

    o bug fix: `seqBGEN_Info()` now seeks to the first variant data block at
      'offset + 4' before probing the phased status, # of bits and ploidy,
      instead of assuming that the block immediately follows the header or
      sample identifier block; previously it crashed on bgen files with
      padding in between, e.g., the UK Biobank imputation files which omit
      the sample identifiers but keep the space reserved


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.5 (2026-06)
-------------------------

    o new `seqGDS2BGEN()` for the reverse conversion from GDS to bgen files
      (layout v1.2), with genotype probabilities sourced from GP (lossless),
      DS (dosage-derived) or GT (hard calls), and zlib/zstd compression

    o define -DHAVE_ZLIB so the header-only bgen compressed-block writer is
      enabled

    o new options 'sp.real8u' and 'sp.real16u' in `seqBGEN2GDS()` to store
      dosages and probabilities in sparse arrays of packed real numbers
      (requiring gdsfmt >= v1.49.9)


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.4 (2025-02)
-------------------------

    o Detect python3 and python2 in Makefile

    o new argument 'ignore.chr.prefix' in `seqBGEN2GDS()`


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.3 (2024-03)
-------------------------

    o fix a C++ compiler issue with the source code of bgen


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.2 (2022-12)
-------------------------

    o update bgen library to v1.1.8 (Jun 27, 2020)

    o `seqBGEN_Info(NULL)` returns the version of bgen library

    o `seqBGEN_Info()` returns additional information: phased status, # of bits,
      and ploidy

    o `seqBGEN2GDS()` outputs to dosages by default, instead of prob.


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.1 (2020-12)
-------------------------

    o new options 'sp.real32' and 'sp.real64' in `seqBGEN2GDS()` to store
      a sparse dosage matrix (requiring gdsfmt >= v1.24.0)


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.9.0 (2018-11)
-------------------------

    o first release of gds2bgen
